                        ],
                        "form": "quaked"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "2ce4e235-38db-44e8-a00d-9899a8acf893",
                        "entry_id": "5661c46b-0ff6-39e1-b843-c30086aff8a6",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "quaked"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c9302ee7-1b47-3e98-b931-6a7fd66edeb0",
                        "entry_id": "5661c46b-0ff6-39e1-b843-c30086aff8a6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To tremble or shake."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "913befef-428a-49d0-a7f5-1e6cff8b92ae",
                                "sense_id": "c9302ee7-1b47-3e98-b931-6a7fd66edeb0",
                                "text": "I felt the ground quaking beneath my feet."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "630f7870-9892-4171-9399-561fb16e7662",
                                "sense_id": "c9302ee7-1b47-3e98-b931-6a7fd66edeb0",
                                "text": "Dorus threw Pamela behind a tree; where she stood quaking like the partridge on which the hawk is even ready to seize.",
                                "translation": "The New Arcadia",
                                "english": "The New Arcadia"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "96c307e3-572c-4ae0-a005-fc3d28d5cf8f",
                                "sense_id": "c9302ee7-1b47-3e98-b931-6a7fd66edeb0",
                                "text": "The mountains quake at him, and the hills melt, and the earth is burnt at his presence."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0dfa2b97-62ac-3a57-8555-7cfb411cdb9a",
                        "entry_id": "5661c46b-0ff6-39e1-b843-c30086aff8a6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To be in a state of fear, shock, amazement, etc., such as might cause one to tremble."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively",
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "620a96f7-0bf2-4949-a211-8ce1a20c5c58",
                                "sense_id": "0dfa2b97-62ac-3a57-8555-7cfb411cdb9a",
                                "text": "Turning back, then, toward the basement staircase, she began to grope her way through blinding darkness, but had taken only a few uncertain steps when, of a sudden, she stopped short and for a little stood like a stricken thing, quite motionless save that she quaked to her very marrow in the grasp of a great and enervating fear."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "aa1d36b7-2eba-455b-853e-be5f2100233f",
                                "sense_id": "0dfa2b97-62ac-3a57-8555-7cfb411cdb9a",
                                "text": "If Cupid have not spent all his quiver in / Venice, thou wilt quake for this shortly."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b41ff8ac-dd57-4dd0-a8df-9c7e2befe184",
                                "sense_id": "0dfa2b97-62ac-3a57-8555-7cfb411cdb9a",
                                "text": "Now could I drink hot blood / And do such bitter business as the bitter day / Would quake to look on."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "23771412-30a4-4687-90c1-a37b080300eb",
                                "sense_id": "0dfa2b97-62ac-3a57-8555-7cfb411cdb9a",
                                "text": "Who honours not his father, Henry the fifth, that made all France to quake, Shake he his weapon at us, and pass by."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ef9d35f2-827c-41f8-a13f-880e4279b369",
                                "sense_id": "0dfa2b97-62ac-3a57-8555-7cfb411cdb9a",
                                "text": "Son of man, eat thy bread with quaking, and drink thy water with trembling and carefulness."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "51afdbd8-cb75-47be-b3aa-67e1f674e652",
                        "source_entry_id": "5661c46b-0ff6-39e1-b843-c30086aff8a6",
                        "source_sense_description": "tremble or shake",
                        "target_lang_word": "beben",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "beben",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7cb403ca-1eff-3730-b0fe-8d08f1e79dbb",
                                        "entry_id": "c8020a5f-97f5-3efd-b472-c97560b5ace4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "stark erzittern"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "beec5417-ae80-4caf-b972-14e2c28b6bb5",
                                                "sense_id": "7cb403ca-1eff-3730-b0fe-8d08f1e79dbb",
                                                "text": "Die Erde bebte von den heranrückenden Panzern."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "05091088-ab08-46fd-bfcf-d028efbf5c00",
                                                "sense_id": "7cb403ca-1eff-3730-b0fe-8d08f1e79dbb",
                                                "text": "Noch mehr aber bebte mein Gegenüber, tief in den Graben gekauert und todesängstig."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5e80de0a-a373-48e5-a178-c06866161b21",
                                                "sense_id": "7cb403ca-1eff-3730-b0fe-8d08f1e79dbb",
                                                "text": "„Die Herzen bebten über die Kühnheit des jungen, schönen, wagemutigen Paares.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "14a7860e-ae69-41b0-8b4c-45b5382ec790",
                                                "sense_id": "7cb403ca-1eff-3730-b0fe-8d08f1e79dbb",
                                                "text": "„Es ist wohl möglich, daß später einmal irgendein besonderer Geist sich findet, der meine anscheinend phantastischen Berichte als nüchterne Selbstverständlichkeiten zu erklären vermag – ein klarer und scharfer Geist, weniger exaltiert als ich, der in den Umständen, die ich mit bebender Scheu enthülle, nichts weiter sieht als die einfache Folge ganz natürlicher Ursachen und Wirkungen.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
